C2C.ENGINES(7)                    C2C Manual                      C2C.ENGINES(7)

NAME
    c2c.engines — the eight whole engines, and the reference that drives them all

DESCRIPTION
    In-process adapters implement the pair of interfaces CacheProvider
    (capture) and CacheInjector (install, generate, score). They are
    discovered through the entry-point group c2c.engines; the registry
    (c2c.integrations.engines) keeps built-in and user entries in
    separate places (c2c.engines(7) — read the manual pages before
    mounting an adapter).

    Engines of the distribution, with notes:

    reference      The house nets, needing the train extra (torch): a
               miniature deterministic Transformer (prefill, capture, install,
               greedy and sampled generation, teacher-forced score).
               The reference implementation of the ABI: what passes here,
               passes everywhere.

    hf             HF Transformers: past_key_values via forward hooks
               and the generation mixin. Full fidelity where the engine
               version exposes the cache API; degrades to prefill-only
               capture (documented) when it does not.

    vllm           vLLM: prefix-cache / KV-connector plugin interface
               (the engine's own connector API). Where no connector is
               found, the adapter degrades to prefill-only capture and
               says so.

    sglang         SGLang: RadixAttention cache hooks.

    tensorrt-llm, tgi, ollama, mlx, llama-cpp
               Per-engine shims. Where the engine exposes no cache hook,
               the adapter falls back to prefill-only capture and
               documents the degradation (see DEGRADATION, printed by
               c2c doctor). No degradation is silent, ever.

    Third parties may ship their own adapters: expose the entry point in
    the group c2c.engines, implement the two interfaces, one ABI, many
    adapters. See the plugin SDK guide in CONTRIBUTING.md.

    Out-of-process, harness-agnostic (the "any harness" guarantee):

    c2c-serve      OpenAI-compatible HTTPS front; virtual model ids of
               the form c2c/<receiver>←<sharer>; streaming SSE; tools
               passed through to the Receiver.

    c2c-mcp        Model Context Protocol server on stdio; tools
               c2c_register_pair, c2c_fuse, c2c_ask; the harness still
               owns the loop.

    A2A bridge     Agent cards advertised beside the text endpoints, so
               multi-harness agent societies can discover
               cache-capable peers.

ACCEPTANCE (spec §4.2)
    The paper's Table 4 accuracies and times, within ±0.5 %, must be
    attainable through each of: the native HF adapter, the vLLM adapter,
    the c2c-serve proxy, the c2c-mcp server. One communication, many
    transports.

SEE ALSO
    c2c(1), c2c.config(5), c2c.fuser(5), the manual of your engine.

